## Why This Is Asked
This tests ability to design governance for cross-team experimentation, balancing speed with reliability and data integrity.

## Key Concepts
- KPI ownership and charter
- Preflight power analysis and data-quality gates
- Guardrails: latency, error rate, quotas
- Feature flags, canary and cohort rollouts
- Artifacts: experiment charter, data map, rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRollout(experiment, metrics) {
  const {power, mde, dataQuality} = metrics;
  if (!experiment.flagsEnabled) return false;
  if (power < experiment.requiredPower) return false;
  if (!dataQuality.ok) return false;
  if (metrics.latency > experiment.maxLatency) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would thresholds vary by product area?
- How would you measure guardrail impact on velocity and reliability?

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design lightweight governance frameworks for multi-team organizations with regional considerations, emphasizing practical artifacts, rituals, and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts

- Engineering governance
- Artifacts and rituals
- Metrics and experiments

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple guardrail filter: decide if a feature request should be evaluated against guardrails
function shouldGuardrailsApply(request) {
  const highImpactPatterns = [/auth|security|data/i];
  return highImpactPatterns.some((r) => r.test(request.description));
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design governance for large microservice ecosystems, including contract testing, versioning, auditability, and risk management under regulatory pressure.

## Key Concepts
- Contract-first API design and governance
- Versioning strategy and backward compatibility
- Contract testing integration (Pact) in CI
- Rollout strategies with canaries/flags and rollback criteria
- Immutable auditing and regulatory compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pact contract test example (Node.js)
const { Pact } = require('@pact-foundation/pact');
const provider = new Pact({
  consumer: 'UserService',
  provider: 'OrderService',
  port: 1234,
  log: './pact.log',
  dir: './pacts'
});

provider.setup().then(() => {
  provider.addInteraction({
    state: 'user exists',
    uponReceiving: 'a request for user details',
    withRequest: {
      method: 'GET',
      path: '/users/123'
    },
    willRespondWith: {
      status: 200,
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: { id: 123, name: 'John Doe' }
    }
  });

  // Test consumer interaction against contract
  return axios.get('http://localhost:1234/users/123');
}).then(() => {
  provider.verify();
}).finally(() => {
  provider.finalize();
});
```
